Numware is a ransomware program for the Numworks calculator.
It's just for fun and doesn't cause any damage to the calculator.
If you enter the wrong key, simply reset your calculator using the button on the back.

In the current code, the private key is `5925cdf68a8d42ce26121d09961bed1d5be657b0b722cf1533a1464f289a4835`.

Make the app with `build.sh`.
You can generate public and private keys with `generate_key.py`.
Put your public key in `src/main.cpp` in variable `str_n`.

It uses AES encryption (symmetric) combined with RSA encryption (asymmetric).

We use :
- [tiny-bignum-c](https://github.com/kokke/tiny-bignum-c)
- [storage.c](https://framagit.org/Yaya.Cout/numworks-extapp-storage/-/tree/master)
